    {
      "issue": "The notice establishes the 2026 adjustment but does not reproduce Regulation 1148's full eligibility conditions or tenant-notice requirements. Coverage remains qualified and awaits execution review; the supplied fact vocabulary also cannot express the exact tenancy-start cutoff and Costa-Hawkins rent-setting condition. Do not treat this record as establishing eligibility or extract a specific notice period from this source.",
      "quoted_span": "The 2026 AGA may not adjust tenants’ rents when their tenancy began on or after \nJanuary 1, 2025, and who had their rents set pursuant to the Costa-Hawkins Rental \nHousing Act.  The Order – Rent Board Regulation 1148 – also sets forth the conditions \nfor qualifying for this rent increase and the notice that must be given to tenants in order \nto raise the rent.",
      "source_doc_id": "D008",
      "source_url": "https://rentboard.berkeleyca.gov/sites/default/files/documents/AGA%20Public%20Notice.pdf",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-01T22:35Z"
    },
    {
      "issue": "January 1, 2026 is the expressly stated earliest date for using this adjustment. October 16, 2025 is the adoption date, not the adjustment's commencement date. The notice does not establish a universal ceiling for every Berkeley rent increase or resolve interactions with other adjustment mechanisms.",
      "quoted_span": "At its regular meeting on October 16, 2025, the Berkeley Rent Stabilization Board \nadopted the Annual General Adjustment (AGA) Order for Year 2026 which will allow \neligible landlords to increase the 2025 permanent rent ceilings by 1.0% no earlier than \nJanuary 1, 2026.",
